  <abstract format="text/plain" language="en" script="Latn">A video sensor is a device used by technology to extract useful information, for example, the number, gender, and age of persons in front of camera, by processing video data captured by camera. Recommendation ITU-T H.742.0 describes an architecture and the requirements of IPTV application events extracted by video sensor devices. The requirements cover general functionalities, delivery mechanisms, metadata, and functions to avoid the risk of privacy infringement.</abstract>
